  "description": "<p>The following sparql query uses a filter to select all the objects having the dc:title expressed in italian (\"it\") language:</p>\n\n<p>select ?o ?t<br/>\nfrom &lt;#ri&gt; <br/>\nwhere {?o &lt;dc:title&gt; ?t .<br/>\nfilter( langMatches( lang(?t), \"it\") )}</p>\n\n<p>The query executed by <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/risearch\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/risearch</a> returns 0 results, while the same query without the filter condition gives the following results:<br/>\n(note: there are several nodes with xml:lang = 'it')</p>\n\n<p>&lt;sparql xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/rf1/result\"&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;head&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;variable name=\"o\"/&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;variable name=\"t\"/&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;/head&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;results&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;result&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;o uri=\"info:fedora/shoah:45651\"/&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;t xml:lang=\"it\"&gt;Intervista a Aldo Isaia Zargani, Rome - Italy&lt;/t&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;/result&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;result&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;o uri=\"info:fedora/shoah:41732\"/&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;t xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;Interview with Miezyslaw Rudnicki, Rome - Italy&lt;/t&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;/result&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;result&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;o uri=\"info:fedora/shoah:24954\"/&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;t xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;Interview with Leo Lev Zelikowski, Montreal - Canada&lt;/t&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;/result&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;result&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;o uri=\"info:fedora/shoah:44169\"/&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;t xml:lang=\"it\"&gt;Intervista a Franco Bemporad, Florence - Italy&lt;/t&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;/result&gt;<br/>\n   <span class=\"error\">&#91;CUT&#93;</span></p>\n\n<p>Which is the correct way to filter on xml:lang with sparql/Mulgara in Fedora 3.1?</p>",
